WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:01.830
Corylus.

00:03.380 --> 00:06.990
Every writing app asks you
to put your novel somewhere.

00:07.460 --> 00:12.910
Inside a database.
Inside a bundle. Inside an account.

00:14.360 --> 00:18.610
And then you can only reach it through
the one application that understands it.

00:19.180 --> 00:22.310
Which is fine, until it is not.

00:23.460 --> 00:29.550
Corylus gives you the binder, the
corkboard, the outliner, the story bible.

00:29.920 --> 00:33.370
Everything a book in two
hundred pieces needs.

00:34.520 --> 00:38.324
And it keeps every chapter
as a plain Markdown file,

00:38.324 --> 00:41.250
in an ordinary folder, on your own disk.

00:41.920 --> 00:45.370
Not as an export. As the actual format.

00:46.520 --> 00:49.650
No account, because there is no server.

00:50.020 --> 00:53.790
Grammar and natural voices
that run on your own machine.

00:54.160 --> 00:59.290
macOS, Windows, iPhone, iPad and Android.

01:01.040 --> 01:03.006
If Corylus vanished tomorrow,

01:03.006 --> 01:08.090
your entire body of work would still
be clean, portable, future-proof text.

01:09.640 --> 01:13.810
Corylus is free.
It is built by one person.

01:14.180 --> 01:16.270
There is a link below.
